## Proposed design
Three coordinated edits making the fast-lane the visually default lane.

1. **New "Choosing a lane" decision rule in `.claude/CLAUDE.md`**, inserted **before** the existing `## SDD Commands` table, anchoring with the verbatim rule and tie-breaker required by AC-1/AC-2.
2. **Reorder Skill routing table** so `/new-quick-feature` and `/new-fix` rows appear above `/new-feature`. Re-label `/new-feature` row to signal "use only when fast-lane criteria don't fit".
3. **Refit the Phase Pipeline ASCII** to a vertical "branch from top" layout: a common `idea` head splits into a `fast-lane` branch and a `full-lane` branch, both first-class. Stays ≤120 cols (matches existing peak); avoids side-by-side blow-out (planner risk #2).
4. **Rewrite `description:` of `new-feature`, `new-quick-feature`, `new-fix`** to encode the lane criteria (AC-5). Hard cap 200 chars; target 120–180.
5. **Reconcile all 7 fast-lane mentions** (lines 91, 118, 203–204, 216, 285 plus diagram) so `grep -n -i 'fast-lane\|quick-spec' .claude/CLAUDE.md` reads as a coherent narrative (AC-4). Manual-only constraint preserved verbatim at line 216.

